      "skill": "engineering-terminology-polishing-zh",
      "language": "zh",
      "prompt": "A research-group editor asks whether the shared bank can now recommend the full term \"weighted cross-entropy loss\" and the Chinese wording \"加权交叉熵损失函数\". They see P92, P96, P97, P100, P111 and P112 in the source records. Give a concise Chinese decision on which records support which scope and what, if anything, remains to check. The editor also proposes making inverse class frequency the mandatory definition and calling P112 a second process-window fault diagnosis experiment. Decide how to handle those proposals from the records, with exact reading locators where useful. This is terminology review, not advice to add a new method or experiment.",
