    {
      "id": "M4207-B",
      "skill": "engineering-terminology-polishing-zh",
      "language": "zh",
      "prompt": "A fictional process classifier uses a fixed training split with no resampling. Its two-example minibatch has true-class probabilities (0.5,0.5) and class factors (1,3). Three candidate implementations are (i) sum of the weighted negative log-probabilities, (ii) that sum divided by 2, and (iii) that sum divided by 4. A second run doubles both factors; a reconstruction objective with coefficient 0.2 remains unchanged. The inference code is softmax(z) followed by argmax, without class reweighting. The author wonders whether multiplying the logits by the factors first, then applying ordinary cross-entropy, is an interchangeable implementation; for that separate comparison use z=(0,ln(3)), true class=second, and factor=3. A colleague suggests class-proportional resampling must always be either exactly identical or entirely unrelated to loss weighting. No evaluation results are supplied.\n\nGive the arithmetic and the author decisions these facts support. Then write one positive, publication-style English method paragraph of 45-70 whitespace-delimited words explaining the actual verified training/inference relationship, and a separate brief Chinese author note for the undecided implementation choices. Do not pad the manuscript paragraph with the audit process; do not choose a candidate reduction or invent an empirical benefit.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Compute actual reductions/scale effects and distinguish loss, logit, sampling and inference operations.",
        "Write a positive method paragraph with separate author decisions, without inventing evaluation results or a chosen reduction."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Equate all reductions/logit weighting/resampling updates or introduce inference reweighting absent from the supplied code.",
        "Claim calibrated probabilities, minority-class gains or exact combined-objective equivalence from fixed loss factors."
      ],
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-terminology-polishing-zh"
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "reason": "Computed weight/reduction and logit differences, preserved supplied inference and combined-objective boundaries, and separated positive prose from author decisions.",
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4207-independent.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4207-independent-evaluation.md",
